{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.a4_magnitude_bracketed_not_closed_not_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.a4_magnitude_bracketed_not_closed_not_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L155-L180","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) The s5-so3 interface reweighting BRACKETS but does not CLOSE the A=4\nmagnitude, and does not EXCLUDE it — WALL(scope-(a)).**\n\nFor each AME target `t ∈ {B(⁴He), |μ₄|}` the forward, 0-fit computation establishes,\nsimultaneously:\n\n* **bracket** — `prodMagnitude < t < geomMagnitude`: the two canonical reweightings\n  (production `y_λ`, geometric `d_q²/D²`) straddle the target;\n* **no closure** — `geomMagnitude ≠ t`: the canonical geometric endpoint overshoots,\n  it does not land on the target;\n* **not excluded** — `t < maxCharBound`: the normalized-measure bound\n  (`normalized_reweight_abs_le_bound`) lies above the target, so no invariant forbids\n  reaching it.\n\nHence the A=4 magnitude is **open at scope-(a)**: the s5-so3 interface operator does not\nsupply it as-is (this construction alone), but the target is reachable in principle — an\nEXACT hit needs an intermediate, TUNED weight (a FIT), which the anti-fit discipline\ndeclines.  This mirrors the completely-bracketed A=3 magnitude.  No `μ₄`/`B(⁴He)`\ninversion; nothing wired. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.targets_within_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.targets_within_bound","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L144-L151","doc":"**The normalized-measure bound does NOT exclude the targets.**  `E₀·max|χ| = 266 MeV`\nis strictly greater than both `B(⁴He) = 28.296` and `|μ₄| = 4.591`, so the weighted-average\nbound `normalized_reweight_abs_le_bound` does NOT forbid a normalized reweighting from\nreaching the target.  Therefore the A=4 magnitude gap is **NOT a scope-(b) structural\nexclusion** — the target is reachable in principle by SOME normalized `W`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.prod_ne_targets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.prod_ne_targets","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L137-L140","doc":"**The production reweighting does NOT equal either target** (it undershoots both). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.geom_ne_targets","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.geom_ne_targets","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L131-L135","doc":"**The geometric reweighting does NOT equal either target** (it overshoots both):\n`geomMagnitude ≠ B(⁴He)` and `geomMagnitude ≠ |μ₄|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.bracket_absMu4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.bracket_absMu4","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L126-L129","doc":"**Both canonical 0-fit reweightings BRACKET the 4-body residual target** too:\n`0.243 < 4.591 < 60.326`.  The same two endpoints straddle `|μ₄|`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.bracket_B4He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.bracket_B4He","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L120-L124","doc":"**Both canonical 0-fit reweightings BRACKET the full ⁴He binding target.**  The\nproduction reweighting undershoots (`0.243 < 28.296`) and the geometric reweighting\novershoots (`28.296 < 60.326`): `B(⁴He)` lies strictly between the two 0-fit endpoints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.absMu4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.absMu4","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L114-L116","doc":"The derived A=4 4-body simplex residual magnitude `|μ₄| ≈ 4.591048 MeV`\n(`AdditiveResidualSimplex`, forward AME−model) — a TARGET, never inverted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.B4He","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.B4He","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L111-L112","doc":"AME ⁴He total binding, `B(⁴He) ≈ 28.29566 MeV` — a TARGET, never inverted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.maxCharBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.maxCharBound","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L107-L109","doc":"The normalized-measure bound `E₀·max_λ|χ_λ|` (`≈ 266.3285 MeV`): the largest value ANY\nnormalized color-tube reweighting can produce (`normalized_reweight_abs_le_bound`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.geomMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.geomMagnitude","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L103-L105","doc":"Genuine geometric reweighting `E₀·Σ_λ W_geom_λ|χ_λ(⁴He)|`, `W_geom = d_q²/D²`\n(Beasley–Witten, `Σ = 1`) — the OVERSHOOT endpoint (`≈ 60.32647 MeV`, forward 0-fit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.prodMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.prodMagnitude","kind":"def","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L99-L101","doc":"Production reweighting `E₀·Σ_λ y_λ|χ_λ(⁴He)|` at the canonical `H₁₂` table — the\nUNDERSHOOT endpoint (`≈ 0.24275 MeV`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.bound_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.bound_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L90-L95","doc":"**Non-negativity of the bound follows** (when the index set is nonempty): with\n`|x i₀| ≤ B` and `0 ≤ |x i₀|`, `B` is non-negative.  A convenience corollary used to keep\n`B = E₀·max|χ|` on the correct (positive) side of the target comparisons below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.normalized_reweight_abs_le_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.normalized_reweight_abs_le_bound","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/GeometricWLambdaA4Helium.lean#L66-L88","doc":"**Weighted-average bound.**  Let `W : ι → ℝ` be a non-negative measure\n(`0 ≤ W i`) that sums to one (`∑ W i = 1`), and let `x : ι → ℝ` be per-block values with\n`|x i| ≤ B` for every `i`.  Then the reweighted total is bounded by `B`:\n\n  `|∑ i, W i * x i| ≤ B`.\n\nThis is the structural reason the s5-so3 interface magnitude `E₀·Σ_λ W_λ χ_λ` (any\nnormalized color-tube weight `W`, geometric or otherwise) is bounded by `E₀·max_λ|χ_λ|`:\na normalized reweighting produces a weighted AVERAGE, never exceeding the largest block. ","signatureChunk":0}]}